To count distinct subsequences, we can use dynamic programming. Let dp[i] be the number of distinct subsequences ending with the i-th character of the string. Then dp[i] = dp[i-1] + dp[i-2] + ... + dp[0], where dp[j] is the number of distinct subsequences ending with the j-th character of the string, and j < i. The base case is dp[0] = 1, since there is only one subsequence of length 0, which is the empty string. The answer is the sum of dp[i] for all i from 0 to n-1, where n is the length of the string. To avoid integer overflow, we can use a long long variable to store the sum.
